  "instructor": [
    {
      "text": "Welcome to the Drone Technology Lab. We will assemble a quadrotor, characterise its motor on the bench, then verify that it can fly.",
      "audio": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Start in Input Parameters — tap any component tile to open its option library. Watch the Diagnostics Log: if the propellers collide or a part is over-rated it will flag an error you must fix.",
      "audio": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Module 1 · Tab 1 shows the assembled drone. Run the Assembly Check to confirm the geometry is sound, then switch to Static Thrust to mount a motor on the bench and measure its thrust.",
      "audio": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Module 2 characterises the motor on the stand: first the thermal test measures RPM loss as the windings heat up, then the efficiency test sweeps throttle to find the best operating point.",
      "audio": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Module 3 is the flight verification. Set a target altitude and run it — the drone flies with real vertical dynamics and reports whether it can hover and climb to your target.",
      "audio": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Outstanding — every experiment is complete. Your reward component is now unlocked in the Outputs panel.",
      "audio": null
    }
